{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Zul'Gurub: High Priestess Jeklik's Bat-tering Charge reaches players out of melee within 25 yards only and her Screech starts where she lands",
  "contract": [
    "The tester reports (live, 2026-11-04) that ranged players and healers at her maximum range are never charged,",
    "while our Jeklik charged players at 30 yards and more: the DBC gives Bat-tering Charge (2106125) 100 yards.",
    "Stock Jeklik's Charge reaches 8-25 yards. Her bat form charges 2 s in and every 20 s after that. The far",
    "hero stands about 35 yards away, the only player out of melee, so no charge comes 2 s in and she screeches",
    "in its place. Then the near hero steps out to about 13 yards from the tank and the next charge reaches them.",
    "Fear Ward keeps the tank and the near hero in place through the first Screech, and the tank attacks again to",
    "hold her attention. The testers of 2026-11-08 and 2026-11-13: on live her Terrifying Screech (2106131) starts",
    "the moment the charge lands (12 of 12 landed charges, 0-9 ms), where she landed; ours moved toward her",
    "victim, the tank, for a world tick or two before the cast stopped her. She lands 1.5 yards (the target's",
    "combat reach) short of the near hero, so her distance to the tank is at most 1.5 yards below the tank's",
    "distance to the near hero; one tick of the old chase at her 15 yards per second adds 0.75 yards or more.",
    "The screech is counted from a snapshot taken after the first, fallback screech has gone off.",
    "Until the tank has engaged her, the other heroes wait about 34 yards away, where the far hero backs off to,",
    "and then come back beside the tank: she aggroes a hero beside her the moment she appears, and a hero she",
    "chased as they backed away would end up in charge range."
  ],
